WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.760
When you think of Venom, you usually think&nbsp;
of the symbiote's main squeeze — Eddie Brock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.600
But another character from Venom lore is making&nbsp;
waves in movies now. Let's peel back the untold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.880
truth of She-Venom, from her dark origins in&nbsp;
comic books to her life on the silver screen.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.280
Anne Weying debuted in 1993's&nbsp;
"The Amazing Spider-Man" #375.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.680
A lawyer once married to Eddie Brock, Anne&nbsp;
is approached by Spider-Man to help track&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.640
down her ex-husband, who's kidnapped Peter&nbsp;
Parker's seemingly-resurrected parents.
 &nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.120
With Anne's help, Spider-Man manages to&nbsp;
trace Venom to an old haunt of Eddie's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.480
the Thrill World amusement park. Anne secretly&nbsp;
tags along and tries to appeal to Venom's sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.520
of reason, but she's interrupted when Eddie&nbsp;
is attacked by Silver Sable's Wild Pack.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.240
While Venom and Spider-Man&nbsp;
fight the Pack together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.040
Anne helps Peter's parents (who turn out to&nbsp;
be robots built by the fiendish Chameleon)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.480
escape. She then returns to&nbsp;
rescue Eddie from being killed.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.960
Things take a dire turn when a damaged&nbsp;
Ferris wheel almost falls on Anne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.760
but Venom, with Spider-Man's help, manages&nbsp;
to rescue her in time. She proceeds to point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.600
out that Spider-Man wouldn't have tried&nbsp;
to rescue her if he were a bad person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:17.680
which finally convinces Venom to stop terrorizing&nbsp;
his longtime foe ... for a while, anyway.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.160
Anne Weying next appears in the 1995 miniseries&nbsp;
"Venom: Sinner Takes All." In this story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:29.040
she gets shot by a new version of the&nbsp;
villainous Sin-Eater. Anne ends up hospitalized,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.080
but is soon whisked away by Venom when the&nbsp;
Sin-Eater tracks her down to finish the job.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.320
The trip to Venom's underground hideout&nbsp;
reopens Anne's stitched-up wounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.840
which leads Eddie to try healing&nbsp;
her by sharing his symbiote.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.320
When that isn't enough, Eddie tells the alien&nbsp;
suit to separate from him for the time being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.960
so it can bond with Anne&nbsp;
completely. Thus, She-Venom is born.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.520
As She-Venom, Anne manages to save Eddie&nbsp;
from two criminals who find his lair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.840
She does this by violently killing them,&nbsp;
however, prompting a horrified Eddie to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.000
blackmail the alien into releasing&nbsp;
Anne and merging with him again.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.960
By that point, Anne is fully healed, but she is&nbsp;
horrified by her actions as She-Venom, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:13.520
once Eddie reveals that the symbiote can't&nbsp;
actually force a person to act against their will.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:18.480
Disgusted by both the symbiote and what it's&nbsp;
revealed about herself, Anne shuns Eddie for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.440
making the alien suit bond with her in their first&nbsp;
place. Despite this, in the series' final issue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.160
Anne briefly becomes She-Venom once again&nbsp;
to rescue Eddie from a sticky situation.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.360
Despite her mixed feelings toward her&nbsp;
ex-husband and his symbiote "friend,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.040
Anne Weying isn't interested in&nbsp;
getting Eddie Brock arrested.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.560
Unfortunately, she still ends up being&nbsp;
forced to cooperate with the police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.600
when they attempt to capture her ex in&nbsp;
1996's "Venom: Along Came A Spider."

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.160
Anne gives Eddie a subtle heads-up when he&nbsp;
tries to call her, leading Eddie's symbiote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.680
to travel through her phone receiver and&nbsp;
temporarily turn Anne into She-Venom once again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.360
This time, however, the symbiote&nbsp;
remains partially attached to Eddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:04.560
leading to a euphoric experience in which Eddie&nbsp;
and Anne experience each other's memories.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.040
Venom rescues Anne from police headquarters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.000
but she is eventually arrested&nbsp;
for acting as his accomplice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.040
Eddie's symbiote travels to Anne by telephone&nbsp;
once more, this time bonding with her fully.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.800
She-Venom proceeds to go to Thrill&nbsp;
World, in the hopes of meeting Eddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.920
but she finds it's become a hideout for crime&nbsp;
boss L.D. 50 and his associates. A showdown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:29.520
between She-Venom, Ben Reilly's Spider-Man,&nbsp;
the police, and L.D. 50's gang breaks out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.680
during which Anne gives Eddie the symbiote&nbsp;
to heal him from injuries ... but not before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.640
getting her fair share of punches and kicks&nbsp;
(not to mention green slobber) in as She-Venom.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:43.920
After L.D. 50's defeat, Eddie admits he still&nbsp;
loves Anne, who states she'd only consider letting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.520
him back into her life if he put his hatred for&nbsp;
Spider-Man and reliance on symbiotes behind him.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.280
Since her debut, Anne Weying has always&nbsp;
made it clear that she cares about Eddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:59.200
even if they're on the outs. The details&nbsp;
of how and when they broke up, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:05.200
seem to vary from comic to comic. 1997's&nbsp;
"Uncanny Origins" #7 suggests that Eddie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.880
narcissism is what ended their marriage,&nbsp;
and that they broke up before Eddie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.960
fired from the Daily Globe newspaper for&nbsp;
mistaking an imposter for the Sin-Eater.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:17.440
It also makes minor changes to how Venom&nbsp;
was reformed, having him and Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.080
save Anne from a falling wall in the city,&nbsp;
rather than a Ferris wheel at a theme park.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.120
2008's "Venom: Dark Origin" suggests things&nbsp;
happened even more differently. It depicts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.120
Anne and Eddie as still being married when&nbsp;
his inaccurate story about the Sin-Eater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.440
was published. It also implies that it was&nbsp;
Eddie's obsession with success that drove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.360
a wedge between him and Anne, eventually&nbsp;
leading to their divorce. Eddie's constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.440
blaming of Spider-Man for his problems,&nbsp;
including his firing, didn't help either.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:48.160
Anne Weying has always liked&nbsp;
being She-Venom a little too much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:53.840
and that terrifies her. By the time her story&nbsp;
reaches 1999's "Amazing Spider-Man" #19,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:59.120
Anne has become afraid to even leave her home,&nbsp;
in case the symbiote appears and tries to bond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.440
with her once more. A poorly-timed visit from&nbsp;
Eddie Brock, who wants to get back together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:09.280
with her so he can regain some sense of normalcy,&nbsp;
makes things even worse. Anne's panic flares to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.320
further heights when she sees Spider-Man swing&nbsp;
by her apartment window in his black costume.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:18.880
Yet what truly ends up being the last straw&nbsp;
for Anne is seeing Eddie transform into Venom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:23.920
to pursue the wall-crawler. This makes Anne&nbsp;
realize that the symbiote isn't with Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:28.560
despite his all-black look — it's right&nbsp;
in front of her. After Venom leaves, Anne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:33.680
mortified by the whole experience, leaps from her&nbsp;
apartment to her death. When Venom returns and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.800
sees what's happened, he swears revenge, thinking&nbsp;
Anne's earlier glimpse of Spider-Man is to blame.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.840
Though Anne Weying has passed away,&nbsp;
her legacy lives on in a son with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:51.840
Eddie Brock's DNA that the symbiote impregnated&nbsp;
her with during one of her stints as She-Venom.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.080
"You serious?"

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:58.720
Believing she won't be able to raise the child&nbsp;
due to her growing paranoia over the symbiote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.960
Anne forces herself to leave her apartment&nbsp;
and give the baby to her father-in-law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.160
Carl Brock, in 2019's "Venom" #12.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:10.720
Though Anne vows she'll return for her son, she&nbsp;
dies before she can make good on her promise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.120
leading Carl to raise him as his own.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:17.520
Neither Anne nor Carl tells Eddie about the&nbsp;
boy. Eddie doesn't manage to meet him until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:22.720
he arrives wounded (and mind-controlled by the&nbsp;
Venom symbiote) at his father's home. Dylan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.160
and Eddie are initially completely&nbsp;
ignorant of their true connection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.680
nor are they aware that Anne unknowingly&nbsp;
transferred the piece of the Venom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.720
symbiote still in her genes to Dylan,&nbsp;
granting him unique powers. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:38.880
however, they learn the truth, and Eddie&nbsp;
begins taking care of his long lost son.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.200
Anne Weying and Eddie Brock are two very different&nbsp;
people. Yet for some reason, the Venom symbiote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:49.360
seems to like merging with Anne almost as&nbsp;
much as it likes bonding with Eddie Brock.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:54.160
An answer, of sorts, to this confounding&nbsp;
riddle is finally given in 2020's "Venom:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.680
The End," which asserts that Anne&nbsp;
Weying is one of the universe's most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.840
suitable beings for bonding with the&nbsp;
symbiote, outside of Eddie Brock.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.760
Not only that, her compatibility's&nbsp;
right on par with that of Tel-Kar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:11.280
a warrior from the Kree Empire who served as the&nbsp;
Venom symbiote's first host, long before the alien&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:17.200
suit ever met Anne Weying or Eddie Brock. Unlike&nbsp;
Tel-Kar, however, who had to rely on scientific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:22.320
enhancement to bond with the symbiote, Anne's&nbsp;
high compatibility level is completely natural.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:26.400
It's never exactly explained why Anne meshes&nbsp;
so well with the symbiote, although it might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:32.160
because, as "Venom: Sinner Takes All" shows, she&nbsp;
can be just as bloodthirsty as Eddie when pushed.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.400
In one alternate reality, Anne Weying becomes&nbsp;
She-Venom under very different circumstances.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:44.480
As detailed in 2020's "Venom" issues #27&nbsp;
and #28, this Anne is the one who bonds with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:49.520
Venom in a dark cathedral, rather than Eddie&nbsp;
Brock, who is already dead in this universe.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:55.200
What's more, She-Venom eventually transforms into&nbsp;
Agent Venom, the identity Spider-Man's longtime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.200 --> 00:08:00.800
friend and ex-bully Flash Thompson assumes in the&nbsp;
main Marvel Universe. Not long after Anne becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:05.920
Agent Venom, her suit produces several other&nbsp;
symbiotes. This is possibly to prepare for this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:11.680
Earth's conquest by Codex, a corrupted version&nbsp;
of Anne's son, Dylan, and his symbiote armada.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:16.000
This version of Anne meets the main Marvel&nbsp;
Universe versions of Eddie and Dylan Brock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:20.000
when they're accidentally teleported into&nbsp;
her universe. The three team up with Anne's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.400
underground group of symbiote resistance&nbsp;
soldiers to defeat Codex and free the Earth.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:30.320
Anne Weying also makes an appearance&nbsp;
in Marvel Comics' Earth-311 continuity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:34.800
in which all of the Marvel superheroes&nbsp;
are active in the year 1602. She shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:41.120
up in the second issue of "1602 Witch Hunter&nbsp;
Angela" as the bride-to-be of one Edwin Brocc.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.280
Unfortunately, this version of Weying&nbsp;
isn't marrying Brocc for his personality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:50.480
but because Brocc has used the Enchantress'&nbsp;
magical elixir to hypnotize her. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.960
Witch Hunter Angela and Serah Anchorton&nbsp;
save Weying from marrying Brocc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.480
who soon loses his head to Angela's&nbsp;
sword when he tries fighting her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.280
Serah as a red, four-legged creature that,&nbsp;
unsurprisingly, looks kind of like Venom.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:08.720
It's hard to say to what extent "Venom: Dark&nbsp;
Origin" is canon to the Marvel Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:13.120
as it doesn't always 100% square with&nbsp;
past events. If the parts that don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:16.800
contradict anything are in continuity,&nbsp;
though, then Anne Weying and Eddie Brock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:21.680
both went to a very famous college in&nbsp;
Marvel lore: Empire State University.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:26.960
Though it only exists in the comics, unlike the&nbsp;
very real SUNY Empire State College in Saratoga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:32.560
Springs, New York, with which it's sometimes&nbsp;
confused, ESU counts many famed Marvel characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:37.840
among its alumni and faculty. Luminaries&nbsp;
including Norman Osborn, the Human Torch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.480
Curt Connors, and Emma Frost have all walked&nbsp;
its hallowed halls at one point or another.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:47.200
The character most associated with Empire&nbsp;
State University, however, is Peter Parker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:53.360
aka Spider-Man. Though Anne Weying is never shown&nbsp;
meeting Peter at ESU, she does meet Eddie there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.040
in "Venom: Dark Origin." She starts a&nbsp;
relationship with him some time after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:01.360
Eddie takes credit for stopping a gang who&nbsp;
attacked them both on the street. Who really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:06.160
rescued Anne Weying and Eddie Brock, you might&nbsp;
ask? Why, none other than Spider-Man, of course.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.960
Venom has appeared in all kinds of&nbsp;
Spider-Man adaptations over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.640
including multiple cartoons&nbsp;
and three live-action movies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:18.720
Yet somehow, She-Venom, who has a strong&nbsp;
connection to Eddie Brock and his symbiote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:24.320
hadn't appeared in any Spider-Man movies&nbsp;
or television series until 2018's "Venom."

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:28.320
Admittedly, she came somewhat close&nbsp;
in 2012's "The Amazing Spider-Man," as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:32.240
Anne Weying is said to be Curt&nbsp;
Connors' lawyer, but she's never shown.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:36.480
Thankfully, the live-action "Venom"&nbsp;
movie corrects that oversight with style.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.480
"I just bit that guy's head off."

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:42.240
Overall, Anne Weying isn't changed&nbsp;
too much in her on-screen debut:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:45.680
She practices law and has a&nbsp;
romantic history with Eddie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.360
Unlike the comics, however, the two break&nbsp;
up before they have the chance to marry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:54.720
as Eddie's snooping as a journalist&nbsp;
unintentionally torpedoes Anne's legal career.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:59.200
When the Venom symbiote possesses Eddie, Anne&nbsp;
becomes one of his staunchest allies, even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:04.400
becoming She-Venom to save Eddie's life. The two&nbsp;
share a kiss while Anne is She-Venom, though they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:10.560
don't fully rekindle their relationship, as she&nbsp;
has moved on and is dating Dr. Dan Lewis instead.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.480
Anne and Eddie's paths cross again in&nbsp;
"Venom: Let There Be Carnage," however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.760
as any Venom fan might have guessed they would.&nbsp;
These two can't escape each other that easily.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:20.880
"Oh, that's bullsh-t!"

